\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Definition}
\title{Cochain and link translations}
\date{2026-11-17}

\p{On the \vocabk{based cochains}{fdip-00SH} of the
uniform torus #{X=(\mathbb Z/N\mathbb Z)^n}, for
#{a\in X} the \newvocab{cochain translation}
and \newvocab{link translation} are
##{(\tau_a f)_I(x)=f_I(x+a),\qquad
       (\tau_a U)_i(x)=U_i(x+a).}
The exterior direction labels are unchanged. These
are the translation actions of the same vertex
group #{X}.}

\p{A \newvocab{fixed-background translation symmetry}
is a #{\tau_a} commuting with #{\extD_U} for the
specified link field #{U}. For a translation #{\tau_a},
\newvocab{link invariance} in the given
coefficient representation means
##{\rho(U_i(x+a))=\rho(U_i(x))}
for every #{x,i}, where #{\rho} is the given
coefficient representation.}
